-- Stage 11b (2 of 5): deals live only in contracts
-- Tom's choices from the review page (https://claude.ai/artifact/DLucB792pjaV87MDs4ufcm), 23 Oct 2026:
-- everything as suggested, except the Formers listed in supabase/.local/11b/choices.txt.
-- Generated by supabase/.local/11b/make_fix.py.
--
-- (a) Records 65 past contracts for 37 Former members who had none: one per Club Card or
--     advertising term on their QuickBooks invoices (dates from the invoice text, qbo_invoice_id set,
--     sponsorship and partnership as advertiser, non-deal invoices skipped), and for 4 with no
--     QuickBooks invoice, one from the end date typed on the business. All is_current = false, so no
--     one changes status (they stay Former) and nothing joins Renewals.
-- (b) ADAM & POTSIE HAIRDRESSING gets a note (Tom's account) and no contract; the antiques market
--     gets nothing.
-- (c) Old text in the deal fields (deal_terms, invoice_number) that is not already on one of the
--     business's contracts or in its notes is appended to businesses.notes under
--     "From the old deal fields (Stage 11b, 24 Oct 2026):".
-- (d) Then every deal copy on businesses is cleared (is_club_card, is_advertiser, membership_type,
--     contract_start, contract_end, contract_amount, contract_currency, deal_terms, invoice_number).
--     Since migration 20261024_001 nothing reads or writes them; v_businesses works them out from
--     contracts. Status stays as it was for every business (checked at the end).
-- Every row it changes is copied to cc_phase0_backup (reason 'stage11b_deals_2026_10_24') first.
-- Undo: supabase/data-fixes/20261024_stage11b_2_deals_undo.sql
-- Run with psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 after migration 20261024_001_stage11b. It refuses to run twice.

BEGIN;

DO $$ BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cc_phase0_backup WHERE reason = 'stage11b_deals_2026_10_24') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'stage11b_deals_2026_10_24 has already been applied';
  END IF;
END $$;

